# Editing `booky/words.json`

Three things here have already broken production. Read before editing.

## 1. Giveaways: APPEND, never replace

`giveaway` is an **ARRAY**. `booky/app.js` → `activeGiveaway()` shows whichever
entry's `start..end` window (inclusive, local midnight) covers today.

**A giveaway may be running right now.** Scheduling the next one must never
overwrite it. Add a new object to the array; leave existing entries alone.

> On 2026-07-29 a future giveaway was written into what was then a single
> `giveaway` slot while giveaway #1 was mid-window. The card disappeared from the
> win screen five days before the end date promised to readers on Reddit and by
> email. Nothing looked broken — no error, the card simply stopped rendering.

- Past entries can stay forever; out-of-range just doesn't render. No cleanup.
- Windows must not overlap; every `tag` must be unique.
- **Never reuse or rename a `tag` after a giveaway has started.** It is written to
  the Resend contact's `last_name` by `api/booky-subscribe.js` and is the only
  record of who entered — it is how the winner gets drawn.
- Never add an on/off flag. Date-driven means nobody has to remember to turn it off.

## 2. Never change today's or past queue slots

Only dates **strictly after today** may be edited (local midnight rollover, same
as `computeDayNumber`). Displaced words go to the tail or another future slot —
never into today or the past. Changing today's word mid-day breaks the saved games
of everyone who already played.

## 3. The live queue IS served from this repo (since 2026-08-08)

`/api/booky-words` serves `booky/words.json` from this repo. Editing the `queue`
here does change the live word.

Before 2026-08-08 it proxied `booky-deploy.vercel.app` and overlaid only
`giveaway` and `wordBooks[].cover`, so queue edits here shipped nothing at all.
`PROXY_UPSTREAM` in `api/booky-words.js` turns that back on.

- Check what players actually receive:
  `curl -s https://90books.com/api/booky-words | python3 -m json.tool | head`
- The `x-booky-words` header should read `local`.

## Pre-flight — run all three before shipping

```bash
python3 scripts/validate_queue_lock.py   # today/past slots unchanged
python3 scripts/validate_winnable.py     # every answer exists in dictionary.json
python3 scripts/validate_giveaway.py     # giveaway array valid; prints what's live
```

All three should pass. They are green in normal operation, so a red one means a
real problem — do not ship past it.
